# Nothing here is required in production.
#
# Driftmail is configured in the browser at /setup — the wizard writes
# everything into the database.
#
# ── production (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# SETUP_TOKEN     claim the instance with this instead of a Cloudflare API
#                 token. Stores no token, so Domains and DNS stay unavailable.
# CONFIG_ENC_KEY  wraps stored credentials at rest under a key that does not
#                 live in the database.
#
# SETUP_TOKEN=
# CONFIG_ENC_KEY=
#
# ── local development ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The claim proves ownership by checking that your token's Cloudflare account
# runs the Worker serving the request. No Worker serves localhost, so that check
# cannot pass locally. Set this to skip it and paste a real token, which is what
# makes the domain and DNS steps usable while developing.
#
# NEVER set this on a deployed Worker. A loopback hostname is also required, but
# the Host header is client-controlled — this variable is the real gate.
#
# DEV_UNSAFE_SKIP_OWNERSHIP=1
